  "decisionVerbatim": "Final dead-code consolidation RC10-DEAD-02, before runtime: Root adopts FOLLOWUP1ecf1f1d's14 D functions in addition to8 from RESULT6856fd5a. Add exact listed source files/symbols only. Two semantic_revision native realization functions remain LIVE: gtl/semantic_revision_publication.ts computes namedSymbol, descriptors preserve it and leaf_invocation_port module[admittedResolution.namedSymbol] invokes them. Do not delete them.\nRoot resolves sole U as realization_refactor with owning HOW synchronization: updatePublicRunProjectionAuthority is an unused non-barrel forwarding helper. Product/package/API do not require this private JS name; existing constructPublicRunProjectionAuthority already constructs exact immutable authorities from complete input/close pair, and parse remains. Delete updatePublicRunProjectionAuthority from code/src/public/run_projection_authority.ts and revise only the relevant lifecycle Update/Transition cell in design/M05_DIRECT_GTL_TRAVERSAL_EXPANSION_DESIGN.md near2485: a changed actual close pair requires a new immutable authority constructed from that pair and the same source Run/Product basis; it does not mutate prior authority or confer append/execution power. Preserve identity/refusal laws and all public type/constructor/parser behavior; do not assert an unexecuted read path produces it. Root inspected body and exact HOW row; this removes a redundant callable name, not required capability. No Product/requirements change.\nThus23 selected declarations across17 source files, plus one exact HOW cell, alongside core lifetime repair. Same rule: if core genuinely consumes a helper naturally, reuse/report instead of rename/delete/reimplement. Remove adjacent exclusively descriptive comments and newly unused imports/private local declarations ONLY when their entire consumer set was those deleted helpers; reference proof must be retained. No ancillary registry/store deletion or unsupported public/dynamic-contract change. No whole files deleted. 14D exactnames/paths from FOLLOWUP should be captured/pinned mechanically against current source before mutation; codegen uses original normal route.\nRequired lifetime test remains. Extra tests for low-impact dead wrapper removal are unnecessary: use compiler/import/calculus/lifecycle/manifest/native-locator/public export gates and existing affected runtime/read/contract tests. Keep native1800s/300s/200turns and separate frozen proof; no script/dependency changes beyond exactRC10identity.",
